Why this is here:
  A pinned, offline fixture for dogfooding vigiles' plugin loader against a
  real Claude Code plugin. We vendor a SNAPSHOT (not a runtime clone) so the
  dogfood test is deterministic and hermetic — no network at test time.

Included (the harness-relevant slice only, NOT the whole repo):
  .claude-plugin/plugin.json   — plugin manifest (no inline hooks)
  hooks/hooks.json             — the SessionStart hook (hooks/hooks.json convention)
  hooks/run-hook.cmd           — the hook entrypoint it shells out to
  hooks/session-start          — the actual setup script (NOT executed by the dogfood)
  skills/{test-driven-development,systematic-debugging}/  — two representative skills

